===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[move]] [[cautiously]] by advancing its front end.
#: {{ux|en|The ship '''nosed''' through the minefield.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[snoop]].
#: {{ux|en|She was '''nosing''' around other people’s business.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[detect]] by [[smell]] or [[as if]] by smell.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Hamlet|act=IV|scene=iii|page=273|passage={{...}} if you finde him not this moneth, you ſhall '''noſe''' him as you go vp the ſtaires into the Lobby.}}
#* {{RQ:Lindsay Age of Consent|year=1962|page=18|passage=Dogs hurried out to '''nose''' Edmund[.]}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Bob Morris|title=Connoisseurship Runneth Over|work=The New York Times|date=2002-10-20|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2002/10/20/style/the-age-of-dissonance-connoisseurship-runneth-over.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Real connoisseurs know that to '''nose''' and taste properly you have to add still water to your tulip-shaped glass so that the alcohol doesn't overwhelm you.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[push]] with one's nose; to [[nuzzle]].
#* {{RQ:Tennyson Holy Grail|poem=Lucretius|page=211|passage=[L]ambs are glad / '''Nosing''' the mother's udder, and the bird / Makes his heart voice among the blaze of flowers: {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[defeat]] (as in a [[race]] or other [[contest]]) by a [[narrow]] [[margin]]; sometimes with ''out''.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To utter in a [[nasal]] manner; to pronounce with a nasal [[twang]].
#: {{ux|en|to '''nose''' a prayer}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=c. 1635|author=[[w:William Cartwright (dramatist)|William Cartwright]]|title=The Ordinary|passage=It makes far better musick when you '''nose''' Sternold's, or Wisdom's meeter.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To furnish with a nose.
#: {{ux|en|to '''nose''' a stair tread}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[confront]]; be closely face to face or opposite to.
# {{lb|en|intransitive|aviation}} To [[dive]] down in a steep angle; to [[nosedive]]
# {{lb|en|intransitive|aviation|nautical}} To travel with the nose of the plane/ship aimed in a particular direction.
#: {{ux|en|The plane is '''nosing up'''!}}
#: {{ux|en|We have to get it '''nosing down'''.}}

